// TEST: OrbIdx Wreath Partial Subscript (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4003
// THE PARTIAL-READ DECISION, pinned. A dense array answers a short subscript
// with a sub-array view, and a rank-r compact SymIdx group refuses one -- but
// it refuses at RUNTIME, inside the interpreter's `indexArray` ("partial
// (sub-array) read of a compact symmetric array"), with the compiled side
// falling through to a raw subscript that is simply wrong. v1 does not copy
// that precedent for wreath classes; it refuses at TYPECHECK, in both backends,
// with the arity that would have worked.
//
// The reason a partial read has no answer here is structural, not a gap: a
// wreath pool's rows shrink per LEVEL, so a fibre of it is not a class this
// type system can spell (peeling a level unties its r_d sub-blocks into a
// JUXTAPOSITION of depth-(d-1) classes -- the §3 lattice, unbuilt). Returning a
// view of the flat pool would hand back a plausible object with the wrong
// shape, which is the silent-wrong-shape outcome this refusal exists to
// prevent. The message names the working route: decompact(W, 0) first, then
// slice the dense result -- exactly what 215 does.
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let g = lambda(x, y) where comm(x, y) -> x * y
let S = method_for(A, A) <@> g |> compute
let h = lambda(p, q) where comm(p, q) -> p + q
let W = method_for(S, S) <@> h |> compute
let bad = W(0, 1)
// EXPECT: typecheck failure — a wreath pool has no partial (sub-array) read.
